  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mutomo Integrated Sustainable Livelihoods Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD started funding Community for Environment forand Development (CED) in June 2007 to implement a food security project in Kenya.  The project is situated in Ikanga location of Mutomo district &#x2013; in the sub-locations of Nduundune, Kiangwa, and Makele. A total of 450 households were selected to form 29 farmer field schools (FFS). The FFS groups were facilitated to identify Natural Resource Management needs in their localities and to work on their private lands and also public land to improve soil and water management, water conservation structures and stabilizing structures.

CED also aims to support the farmers in crop production and livestock production including provision of drought tolerant seeds such as cow peas, pigeon peas and beans and fruit tree seedlings of mango and avocado. The project also provides Galla goats.

In 2008, the project also supported community water projects including scooping of identified shallow wells. Connecting water to a homestead of an HIV/AIDS support group enabled the group to water their tree nurseries and Aloe Vera plants used for medicinal purpose.</narrative>
  </description>
